---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-file-upload</code> collects files: drop them on the zone, or click it (or press Enter or
  Space) to open the system file picker. Chosen files are listed with their name, size and a remove
  button. The component uploads nothing itself; read <code>files</code> when it fires
  <code>change</code>, or submit it with a form.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 420px;'>
    <wc-file-upload id='file-upload-demo' label='Attachments' multiple></wc-file-upload>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#file-upload-demo').addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('change: ' + event.detail.files.map(function (file) { return file.name; }).join(', '));
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Limits</h3>
<p>
  <code>accept</code> takes the same list as a native file input (<code>.pdf</code>,
  <code>image/png</code>, <code>image/*</code>). <code>max-size</code> is the largest size of one
  file in bytes, and <code>max-files</code> the most files the list holds with
  <code>multiple</code>. Files that do not fit are not added: a short message lists them under the
  zone, and <code>reject</code> fires with <code>detail.files</code>, each a
  <code>{'{ file, reason }'}</code> where <code>reason</code> is <code>'type'</code>,
  <code>'size'</code> or <code>'count'</code>. Without <code>multiple</code>, a new file replaces
  the chosen one.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 420px;'>
    <wc-file-upload
      id='file-upload-limits'
      label='Photos'
      accept='image/*'
      multiple
      max-files='3'
      max-size='2000000'
      helper-text='Up to 3 images, 2 MB each'
    ></wc-file-upload>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#file-upload-limits').addEventListener('reject', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('reject: ' + event.detail.files.map(function (entry) {
        return entry.file.name + ' (' + entry.reason + ')';
      }).join(', '));
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
